"{{Term/Store|Medicinal Molduga||Series, BotW}}" is a [[Side Quest]] in {{BotW}}.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Medicinal Molduga}}<br/>{{Color BotW|Side Quest|Gerudo Town}}|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref>

==Overview==
"Medicinal Molduga" is one of four [[Side Quest]]s that must be completed in order to receive the [[Thunder Helm]] from [[Riju]] as part of "[[The Thunder Helm]]". [[Link]] can obtain it by speaking to [[Malena]] at the [[Gerudo Town]] [[Barracks]], who will be begging [[Babi]] for help.<ref>{{Cite|Please...|Malena|BotW}}</ref>

Malena explains that she recently married the man of her dreams, [[Platt]], but he became sick with a rare illness.<ref>{{Cite|I... I finally found the voe of my dreams, and I just recently married him... I thought I had finally found happiness... But then...my husband fell ill with a rare disease... One difficult to cure.|Malena|BotW}}</ref> To heal her husband, Malena requires [[Molduga Guts]], though she is unable to defeat a [[Molduga]] to obtain any.<ref>{{Cite|The only thing that can save him is the {{Color BotW|Blue|guts of a Molduga}}... But I would never be able to take down such a creature myself...|Malena|BotW}}</ref> She tried to ask for help from the [[Gerudo Soldier]]s, but she realizes it is foolish to expect anyone to face such a dangerous [[Monster]] on her behalf.<ref>{{Cite|I asked the soldiers for help, but... Why would they want to help me? The {{Color BotW|Blue|Molduga}} is a menacing beast... None who face one escape unscathed... So perhaps it's foolish to expect anyone to stick their neck out for a stranger...|Malena|BotW}}</ref> Malena is ashamed to have had to return to Gerudo Town to seek help.<ref>{{Cite|I thought I'd finally gotten out of this town... Never thought I'd have to come crawling back...|Malena|BotW}}</ref>

If Link asks about Molduga, Malena describes them as savage creatures that are avoided by other [[Monster]]s, often found in the [[Toruma Dunes]] and the [[Southern Oasis]].<ref>{{Cite|[Molduga?] The {{Color BotW|Blue|Molduga}} is a monster... A terror so savage that even other monsters won't approach it... It's often been spotted west of here, in the {{Color BotW|Blue|Toruma Dunes}}, and in the south.|Malena|BotW}}</ref> In addition, she shares that they are sensitive to vibrations and attack anything that comes close to them.<ref>{{Cite|It's very {{Color BotW|Red|sensitive to vibrations}}, and it tends to attack anything that draws near.|Malena|BotW}}</ref> Since they can not be approached nor can anyone be used as bait, Malena wonders what she is to do.<ref>{{Cite|You can't approach it or even move near it... And you can't use someone as bait... So what am I to do...|Malena|BotW}}</ref>

Molduga can be found in four different places in the [[Gerudo Desert]]. These locations are the Toruma Dunes, the Southern Oasis, [[North Dragon's Exile]], and [[Arbiter's Grounds]]. Molduga can be fought while [[Shield Surfing]] with the help of a [[Sand Seal]]. They can also be fought by detonating [[Bomb]]s or shooting [[Bomb Arrow]]s near it. Either one of these strategies creates enough vibration to cause a Molduga to fly out of the sand, where it can be stunned and become vulnerable to Link's attacks.

Once Link defeats a Molduga and obtains Molduga Guts, he can return to Gerudo Town to give them to Malena.<ref>{{Cite|[Here, take 'em.] Wait, these... {{Color BotW|Blue|Molduga guts}}! {{Big|You... You'll give these to me?}}|Malena|BotW}}</ref> She thanks Link by rewarding him with a [[Gold Rupee]], as it is all she has to give him.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Oh, sarqso!}} This is all I have to thank you with, but I insist you take it.|Malena|BotW}}</ref> Malena is brought to tears at the thought of saving Platt,<ref>{{Cite|{{Small|This will save him... *sniff*}}|Malena|BotW}}</ref> and the Side Quest will be completed.

